meta {
  name: Create Reference
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/references
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  image: @file()
  description: Gree Comfort Pro 3.5 kW oldalfali klíma telepítés
  is_visible: true
}

script:post-response {
  const createdId = res.body?.id ?? res.body?.[0]?.id;
  if (res.status === 201 && createdId) {
    bru.setVar("referenceId", createdId);
  }
}

docs {
  # Create Reference
  Validates and uploads a reference image to Supabase Storage and creates a new reference record. Performs both MIME type filtering and `sharp` binary header inspection (`jpeg`, `png`, `webp`, and `avif` / `heif` with `av1` compression).

  ### Authentication
  - **Bearer Token** required (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`).

  ### Request Body (`multipart/form-data`)
  - `image` (file, required): Image file (`image/jpeg`, `image/png`, `image/webp`, or `image/avif`; maximum **10 MB**).
  - `description` (string, optional): Caption or description of the installation.
  - `is_visible` (string, optional): Set to `"true"` to publish immediately on the public site (parsed via `is_visible === 'true'`).

  ### Responses
  - `201 Created`: Returns the newly created reference object.
  - `400 Bad Request`: Missing image file, Multer upload error, or database insertion error.
  - `401 Unauthorized`: Missing or invalid JWT token.
  - `413 Payload Too Large`: File exceeds the 10 MB limit (`{ "message": "A kép mérete legfeljebb 10 MB lehet." }`).
  - `415 Unsupported Media Type`: Invalid image binary or unsupported format (`{ "message": "Nem támogatott képformátum." }`).
}